# Keep the Docker build context lean; the image installs and builds from
# scratch. There is deliberately only ONE ignore file: BuildKit would let a
# `docker/Dockerfile.dockerignore` override this one, which is an easy way to
# end up shipping a context nobody meant to.
.git
.github
node_modules
**/node_modules
out
release
doc
# esbuild.mjs stages these into out/examples/ (Help ▸ Examples)
!doc/public/examples/tutorials
!doc/public/examples/tutorials/*.zip
!doc/public/examples/tutorials/LICENSE
images
test
# Icon *sources* and the TikZ pipeline; only icons/app/*.png is built against.
icons/tikz-app
icons/tikz-os
icons/tikz-ui
icons/svg-ui
icons/build-ui
.vscode
*.log

# Kept on purpose, despite looking incidental:
#   CHANGELOG.md      — esbuild copies it into out/ for the What's New dialog
#   icons/app/*.png   — the Linux window icon and electron-builder's app icon
#   doc/public/examples/tutorials/*.zip + LICENSE — esbuild stages them into
#                       out/examples/ for Help ▸ Examples (the build throws without)
